rockchip-vaapi (3.5.0-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Release 3.5.0 Number Nine "Pepper SGT": 4K60 AV1 in Firefox and clean
    AV1 starts in Chrome/Chromium.
  * AV1 with librockchip-mpp1 +pd32 or later on RK3588 (Plaid Pi's build):
    a picture the player syncs early (Firefox, FFmpeg) is decoded once and
    its reference slots committed afterwards, instead of being decoded
    twice. Other MPP builds decode it twice as in 3.0.0 (KI-14). Measured
    on an Orange Pi 5B with Firefox 157: YouTube 4K60 AV1 dropped 91-95 %
    of frames with 3.0.0 and about 8 % with 3.5.0; 1.2-1.5 % after
    start-up with media.video-queue.hw-accel-size = 10 (about 4 % over a
    whole run).
  * Chrome/Chromium AV1: a new decoder decodes its first 25 shown pictures
    before vaEndPicture returns (RKVA_PACE_START), and vaEndPicture is paced
    two pictures behind the decoder (RKVA_PACE). No green or old frames
    seen at playback start or quality switches in 10 measured first plays
    (the earlier candidate: 6 of 10), with MPP +pd32. A rare old frame
    mid-stream remains, as in 3.0.0 (KI-16).
  * All codecs: AV1 pictures go to MPP from a per-decoder thread and come
    back through an output thread; vaSyncSurface waits for the decoder
    instead of polling every 1 ms (RKVA_SYNC_POLL=1 restores polling).
    8-bit frames are exported as MPP's own buffer for clients that export
    after decoding (Firefox, mpv), with no copy (RKVA_ZERO_COPY=0 to turn
    off).
  * Review fixes (rc4): a decoded frame is installed only if its surface was
    not re-targeted meanwhile; vaSyncSurface on the monotonic clock; the
    start window ends at its first capped wait.
  * New switches, all documented in README: RKVA_ZERO_COPY, RKVA_SYNC_POLL,
    RKVA_PACE, RKVA_PACE_START, RKVA_PACE_START_MS, RKVA_AV1_NO_DEFER.
  * Vendor string: Rockchip MPP VA-API Driver 3.5.0 Number Nine "Pepper SGT"
    (defcom5). Named after Number Nine's Pepper SGT co-processor board of
    1987.

