rockchip-vaapi (3.5.0~rc2-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Release candidate 2 for 3.5.0.
  * AV1: pace vaEndPicture for a client that never waits on its pictures
    (afbec6b). Chromium syncs a surface only when it imports it and then
    composites its dma-buf unsynchronised; with the submit thread of rc1 it
    could run up to 16 pictures ahead of the decoder and showed old pictures,
    or green on a surface's first use, at start, seek and loop. Until a
    decoder's client waits on a picture it rendered (vaSyncSurface, or an
    export after decoding: mpv, Firefox, FFmpeg with a download), and again
    after 32 pictures without such a wait, vaEndPicture returns once the
    picture from two pictures earlier is in its surface. RKVA_PACE=n sets
    the depth, 0 turns pacing off. AV1 only.
  * Pacing review follow-ups (c913790, d344183, 104e812): pacing also works
    without the output thread (RKVA_SYNC_POLL=1); the wait is capped at
    150 ms (300 ms for a decoder's first pictures) on a monotonic clock and
    logged as one summary line per 600 pictures; a re-targeted surface ends
    a wait at once; DestroySurfaces waits for vaSyncSurface/pacing waiters
    before destroying a surface's condition variable.
  * Docs: why and when AV1 pacing applies, RKVA_PACE (97cf350, 0606344);
    KNOWN-ISSUES KI-15: the newest AV1 picture of a client that never waits
    is still held until its successor (same as 3.0.0).

